-
-From v105 every leaf counts real entries and fictitious units, and is critical when their sum reaches the capacity C.
-The reserve is always active; there is no switch to disable it.
-
-- **Creation.** The first leaf of an empty tree starts with `rootReserve` units. Each leaf split adds `splitReserve`
-  units, divided between the two halves so that the larger half is as small as possible; equal plans are chosen at
-  random from a generator seeded with `choiceSeed`. Replenishment is permanent: splits keep adding units after real
-  history starts being discarded.
-- **Insertion into a critical leaf.** A leaf holding fictitious units releases one instead of splitting. Otherwise it
-  first moves entries to an adjacent leaf with room, and splits only when neither neighbour can take them.
-- **Pressure fusion.** When an insertion needs a node and there is no free node, no retired node and no free index
-  page, the tree merges two adjacent leaves under the same parent whose real entries fit `pressureMergedLimit`,
-  removing fictitious units as needed. Candidate pairs are indexed, and the pair with the most reclaimable capacity
-  (2C minus the real entries of both leaves) is taken first. Only when no pair qualifies does the allocator advance the
-  floor and reclaim by age.
