-## v107: one unified pool (2026-10-12)
-
-The key/index split is removed. The pool has one index range: B+ nodes and key blocks share its pages, a key block
-being a node slot whose age-list use is `Heap`. `PagePool::configurePartitions` becomes `configureIndexPool`, every
-tree is built that way, and `MemoryConfig` keeps only the backing.
-
-**The structural check (`verify`).**
-- A key block in the age list is a node slot that is not allocated as a node. Its block is found again by
-  `findKeyBlock` from its identifier, and its newest CV equals the age entry's.
-- The heap's oldest block carries the smallest newest CV of all key blocks.
-- Every slot of every node page is a tree node, a key block or a free node, and `live` counts nodes and key blocks.
-- The increasing page identifier is no longer checked. A block identifier is `{incarnation, age index}`, not a
-  sequence.
-- The free-node identities count key blocks: free nodes plus key blocks fill the index pages.
-
-**Cases rewritten.**
-- `partitionConfigurationAndExhaustion` checks the index pool:
-  - every page goes to index requests and none to key requests;
-  - exhaustion and `hasAvailable` behave for both uses;
-  - released pages can all be acquired again;
-  - an oversize key is rejected before any mutation.
-- `keyRequestCannotTakeNodePage` becomes `keyBlocksShareNodePages`. A key block takes a free slot of a node page,
-  the pool hands out no key page, and the identifier stops resolving once the block is released.
-- `workloadReversalsKeepPartitions` becomes `workloadReversalsShareSlots`: slots change role in both directions.
-- `heapReclamationKeepsLiveHintAddresses` reclaims key blocks through an index request. Every pool page and every free
-  node is held, so the request must retire the oldest key blocks.
-- `pendingHintPageStaysOwnedUntilBatchEnd`:
-  - The trigger is an index request.
-  - When keys need blocks before the grouped search (K0, inline-only off), the reclaimer supplies one held node from
-    another page.
-  - The victim page ends with no tree node, and with only the key blocks that its old entries still need.
-- `indexReclamationUsesAgeList` first retires the key blocks that precede the victim node in the age list.
-- `reclamationDuringReservation` and its shared-prefix variant require key blocks to be used and reclaimed, all
-  through index requests.
-- `inlineOnlyMixedEndpoints` counts one key block instead of one heap page.
-
-**Cases restricted, and new ones.**
-- `stableHintLeafReusedAsLeaf` and `stableHintIncarnationSaturates` now run only when their fill keys stay inline,
-  as `stableHintGroupedMatchesScalarUnderIndexReclamation` already did. In K0 and inline-only-off builds, the freed
-  node is taken first by a key block.
-- `stableHintLeafReusedAsKeyBlock`, in every build: a hinted leaf freed and taken as a key block has its incarnation
-  advanced, the hint is rejected as stale, and the write goes to the right leaf.
-- `stableHintSaturatedNodeRefusedAsKeyBlock`, in every build: a free node at `UINT32_MAX` is refused as a key block
-  with `std::overflow_error`, and key-block and free-node counts are unchanged.
-
-**The other B+ batteries.**
-- `ExceptionAgeOrderTests` counts key blocks instead of heap pages in the age list.
-- `UnifiedKeyBlockTests`, `WriteTwoPassTests`, `WriteTwoPassEquivalence`, `FictitiousLeafTests` and
-  `FictitiousPrehistoryTests` lost their split-pool arms.
-- `UnifiedKeyBlockTests` also lost its cases on the removed prefetch-address path and the tree export.
-
-**Results.**
-
-| battery | result, in each of the seven builds |
-|---|---|
-| `BTreeTests` | 111/111 |
-| `UnifiedKeyBlockTests` | 12/12 |
-| `FictitiousLeafTests` | 23/23 |
-| `FictitiousPrehistoryTests` | 5/5 |
-| `ExceptionAgeOrderTests` | 13/13 |
-| `WriteTwoPassTests` | pass |
-
-- The seven builds are default (C23, K64, inline-only), ASan/UBSan, no counters, C15, K32/C31, K0 and inline-only off.
-  ASan/UBSan was clean.
-- The one compiler warning, an unused variable in `PagedBTreeConflictSet.cpp`, was already in 7660f7c10c.
-- `WriteTwoPassEquivalence`'s 600-batch dump is byte-identical to 7660f7c10c's unified pass run on its own. In
-  7660f7c10c's file that pass ran after the split pass in the same process, so it inherited FDB's thread-local random
-  state. That changed split and fusion counts, never the stored intervals or their hash.
-
-**Mutation checks** (scratch copies, `BTreeTests` and `UnifiedKeyBlockTests`):
-
-| mutant | result |
-|---|---|
-| `hasAvailable` true for key requests | 110/111, `partitionConfigurationAndExhaustion` |
-| a released index page not returned to the free list | 109/111: `partitionConfigurationAndExhaustion` (pages not acquired again), and `std::bad_alloc` in `pendingHintPageStaysOwnedUntilBatchEnd` |
-| key requests served index pages | 109/111, `keyBlocksShareNodePages` and `partitionConfigurationAndExhaustion` |
-| the batch's record-size validation removed | 110/111 and 11/12, `partitionConfigurationAndExhaustion` and `rejectBeforeMutation` |
-| a saturated node accepted as a key block | 110/111, `stableHintSaturatedNodeRefusedAsKeyBlock` |
-| acquired index pages not taken from `freePages` | 14/111, the budget identity in `verify` |
-| index pages handed out in reverse order | 111/111 and 12/12: **equivalent for decisions**; only addresses change |
-
-The first two mutants survived until the checks on `hasAvailable` and on acquiring released pages again were added.
-
-**Not covered here.**
-- HugeTLB backing (see its own report).
-- The startup error for the removed knobs, and `BY5_UNIFIED_KEY_BLOCKS` with the pool backing `heap`, which the
-  integration checks cover.
-- A free node whose incarnation is saturated is refused as a key block, with an error. The node goes back to the head
-  of the free list, so later key requests meet it again. Reaching that state takes 2³² allocations of one slot; it is
-  covered here only by setting the counter.
